   "answer": "Last week, the Atlas steering committee met on Monday 19 October 2026. The attendees were Priya Nair, Bob Lindqvist, Sam Ortega, Theo Marchetti, and Dana Whitlock. During the meeting, several decisions were made, including moving the cutover from Monday 9 November 2026 to Monday 16 November 2026 due to a slipped vendor data export. Theo Marchetti was appointed as the new Atlas owner when Dana leaves. The budget was on track with a total of $240k, $60k for the contractor line, and an average of $16.4k per month for cloud spend [1].\n\nAdditionally, there were actions planned, such as Bob Lindqvist confirming the rollback plan by Friday and Theo shadowing Dana on vendor calls. The handover plan for Dana's departure was also discussed, with the last day at Fernhill set for Friday 13 November 2026. Theo Marchetti would take over the Atlas (warehouse migration) area, with the cutover on Monday 16 November 2026 and a runbook in the Atlas folder [4]. \n\nIn another conversation, Sam Ortega and Dana Whitlock discussed the contractor data-quality work, which was dropped with Bob Lindqvist's agreement. Sam Ortega also mentioned the travel budget for offsites being frozen until January [5].",
